            <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-weight:700;font-size:2rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">What we actually do</h2>

            <h3 style="font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 .5rem;">Fix your business record everywhere it appears</h3>
            <p style="line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">We audit your name, address, phone, and hours across Google, Bing, Apple Maps, Yelp, the BBB, Nextdoor, and the local Chamber. Mismatches make an AI hedge instead of naming you. We claim what is unclaimed and correct what is wrong.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 .5rem;">Complete and work your Google Business Profile</h3>
            <p style="line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Every field filled, services listed, real customer questions seeded into the Q&amp;A section, and a review request flow so new reviews keep arriving. Reviews are one of the strongest signals there is, and recency counts.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 .5rem;">Mark up your site so it can be read, not guessed at</h3>
            <p style="line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Structured data telling engines what you do, where you do it, what it costs, and what your customers ask. Plus crawler access so AI systems are allowed to read your site in the first place.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 .5rem;">Rewrite your key pages to answer first</h3>
            <p style="line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">"A standard water heater install takes most of a day and runs $1,100 to $1,800 around here" is quotable. "We pride ourselves on quality workmanship" is not. We rewrite your highest-intent pages so the answer comes first and the sales copy comes second.</p>

            <h3 style="font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 .5rem;">Measure it every month, in writing</h3>
            <p style="line-height:1.75;">We ask ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Mode, and Claude the ten questions your customers ask, and score whether you were named, mentioned, or absent. You get one page: your score, the trend, screenshots, and the competitors named instead of you.</p>
